  "notes": [
    "Maximums and minimums are per every 1,000 points unless otherwise stated (p. 179). The builder applies them as written, which is right for armies up to 1,000 points; scale them up yourself for larger armies.",
    "Grenz cost 43 points in the stat table (p. 178) but 40 in the Line Infantry Brigade box (p. 179); Cavalry Artillery has Stamina 1 in the stat table but 2 in the chapter (p. 73). The builder uses the stat table.",
    "Only the 25% reserves cap on Reserve Artillery is checked; the book doesn't say which other brigades count as 'Abteilung and Army Support'."
  ],
  "specialRules": [
    "Austrian commanders roll Personal Qualities on their own table: 1-2 Low, 4-5 Normal, 6 High (as printed; it doesn't give a 3).",
    "Regimental Orders: an Austrian brigade commander can't order a whole brigade. He orders units individually, except infantry battalions of the same Infantry or Grenz Regiment, cavalry of the same Cavalry Regiment, or Grenadier battalions of the same brigade, each within 6\" of each other.",
    "Austrian Divisional Commanders can order a brigade-sized formation, at -1 to their Staff Rating for each unit over the second in it.",
    "Flintenkartasche: musket-armed infantry in close formation gain an extra shooting dice the first time they shoot at close range.",
    "Line infantry: Lie Down, May Form Square or Battalion Mass/Divisional Mass, Column of Companies, Close Column and Poor Mixed Formation. Grenz add Rifle Mixed Formation, Light Infantry Mixed Formation, Skirmish and Flintenkartasche; Jäger have Light Infantry Mixed Formation and Skirmish.",
    "Austrian cavalry can use Cavalry Deep Formation and Cavalry Mixed Formation.",
    "Abteilung: any cavalry regiment can be replaced by 2, 3 or 4 Small units (Abteilungen) of the same regiment.",
    "Cavalry Artillery moves by horse as on p. 33 of the Black Powder rulebook, but 15\" rather than 18\"."
  ],
